            "week": 1,
            "title": "Introduction to HTML5",
            "lesson_type": "reading",
            "order": 1,
            "content": "HTML (HyperText Markup Language) is the standard markup language for creating web pages. HTML5 introduced semantic elements that give meaning to your content.\n\n## Key Concepts:\n\n**Semantic Elements**: Tags like `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, and `<footer>` describe the purpose of content.\n\n**Document Structure**: Every HTML page starts with `<!DOCTYPE html>` followed by `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>` tags.\n\n**Accessibility**: Using semantic HTML helps screen readers understand your page structure, making the web more inclusive.\n\n## Example:\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <title>My First Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <h1>Welcome to HTML5</h1>\n    </header>\n    <main>\n        <p>This is my content.</p>\n    </main>\n</body>\n</html>\n```",
            "duration_minutes": 15
        }
    },
